WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:32.590
TIKTOK BANS:
On 

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:40.090
June 29, 2020, India announced that they would
ban 59 Chinese apps including TikTok.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:47.020
At first, many speculated that this was just
a scare tactic, and that the ban wouldn’t

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.250
last that long.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:55.039
But, 2.5 years later, TikTok is still banned
in India, and it doesn’t seem like that

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:57.540
will be changing anytime soon.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.220
Around the same time that India banned TikTok,
president Donald Trump was making a lot of

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.019
commotion about banning TikTok as well.

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:09.490
He actually nearly succeeded given that he
introduced an executive order that banned

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:13.090
software updates and transactions through
TikTok.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:17.650
This order didn’t accomplish all that much
though as president Joe Biden would swifty

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.229
revoke this order after taking office.

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:26.640
Since then, it seemed like the whole era of
TikTok fears was finally coming to an end.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.590
More and more creators would expand to TikTok
or completely switch to the platform.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:37.320
And for a brief period, TikTok even became
the most popular site in the world beating

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.490
out Google.com.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:44.590
It very much seems that TikTok is here to
stay like WhatsApp, YouTube, and Instagram.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:50.460
But, more recently, it appears that TikTok
fears have started to ramp up once again.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:56.079
At the end of 2022, congress banned TikTok
across all federally owned devices.

00:01:56.079 --> 00:02:01.539
And since then, this ban has expanded to basically
every institution that’s even vaguely related

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:02.750
to the government.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.729
This includes dozens of states and public
schools and colleges like the University of

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:09.220
Oklahoma and even UT Austin.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.530
There’s even a push from the FCC to completely
ban the app from both the Apple app store

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.560
and the Google play store.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.890
And given that Apple didn’t hesitate to
ban Fortnite a few years ago, they probably

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:26.440
wont hesitate to ban TikTok especially if
they have government support.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:31.530
But, likely the biggest threat for TikTok
is the fact that both sides of Congress are

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.060
now taking this issue seriously.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:38.580
In December, a democratic senator suggested
that Donald Trump may have been right about

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:42.700
TikTok and that the sooner we bite the bullet,
the better.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:49.560
So, banning TikTok is no longer just a right
wing talking point, and the US is by no means

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.680
the only country having these talks.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.530
In fact, China themselves doesn’t allow
the global version of TikTok to be used within

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.780
their country.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.540
So, why is TikTok getting banned around the
world?

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:10.530
SHADY HISTORY:
Well, the answer isn’t rocket science.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:15.110
The reason that TikTok is getting banned is
because it’s considered a national security

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:21.040
threat, but if that was the case, how was
TikTok able to get so large in the first place.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.790
Why wasn’t TikTok banned right from the
start or atleast much earlier than now?

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.770
Well, to answer this, we’ll have to take
a look back at the origins of TikTok which

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:36.269
date back to 2012 when a young engineer named
Zhang Yiming established a company called

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:38.110
ByteDance in Beijing.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:43.540
ByteDance’s first app called Neihan Duanzi
came out in March of 2012.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:48.781
This app centered around sharing funny jokes
and memes, and while seemingly harmless, there

00:03:48.781 --> 00:03:52.180
was something much more sinister going on
in the background.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:57.360
Like Facebook and Google, the app was very
much focused on collecting user data.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.470
This wasn’t Zhang’s first rodeo either.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.930
Before founding ByteDance, Zhang was developing
an app that could use user data to serve them

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.489
news articles that they would be fond of.

00:04:07.489 --> 00:04:12.640
Zhang simply modified these algorithms to
work with memes and funny videos, and this

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.380
was a roaring success.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:20.639
Within 6 years of launch, the app would be
able to reach a whopping 200 million users.

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:25.280
It turns out that when you show people what
they want to hear, it’s quite easy to garner

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.389
their attention.

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:30.919
We’ve seen a very similar phenomenon in
the US which has led to the creation of echo

00:04:30.919 --> 00:04:32.880
chambers across social media.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:39.010
But, this success didn’t last all that long
given that the CCP would step in.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:44.780
In 2018, the CCP would ban Neihan Duanzi for
being too vulgar.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:50.270
And while its true that the app did circulate
a bunch of dirty jokes and memes, this was

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.800
likely not the real reason for its ban.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.139
The real reason came down to two things.

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:59.639
One, the app was circulating memes that poked
fun at the Chinese government calling the

00:04:59.639 --> 00:05:01.440
president Winnie the Pooh.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:06.310
And two, China prefers that their citizens
are generally doing productive things and

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:10.950
this app could not be described as productive
by any stretch of the imagination.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:17.449
So, that was the end of Neihan Duanzi, but
ByteDance likely didn’t mind too much because

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:20.040
they had something much bigger in the works.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:25.370
You see, two years before Neihan Duanzi got
banned, ByteDance launched another app called

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:28.680
Douyin which is the original Chinese version
of TikTok.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:34.770
Initially, Douyin was widely known as the
Musical.ly ripoff, but that was honestly more

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:40.050
of an insult given that Douyin was much more
powerful that Musical.ly ever was.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.050
The reason?

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:44.259
Well, Douyin was built to get users addicted.

00:05:44.259 --> 00:05:49.550
Zhang used all of his experience from his
news app and his meme app to concoct an irresistible

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:50.569
app.

00:05:50.569 --> 00:05:55.130
It played into many of our primal instincts
like our desire for instant gratification

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.380
and constant stimulation.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:02.880
Later in 2016, Douyin would launch outside
of China under the name TikTok.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:08.430
About 1 year later, ByteDance would go ahead
and acquire Musical.ly for $1 billion.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:13.060
And shortly after, they would merge the two
apps together giving rise to the TikTok that

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.289
we all know today.

00:06:15.289 --> 00:06:22.280
BANS PHASE 1:
Almost instantaneously, TikTok caught the

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:27.590
attention of regulators and country officials
but likely not for the reason that you would

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:28.590
expect.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:31.669
The initial concern wasn’t even national
security.

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:34.530
The initial concern centered on the content
itself.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:40.190
To put it bluntly, many countries felt that
TikTok encouraged braindead behavior amongst

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:41.530
young people.

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:47.250
And objectively speaking, this is true given
that we would see trends like devious licks.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:51.979
Some countries also felt that much of TikTok’s
content was obscene, immoral, and vulgar.

00:06:51.979 --> 00:06:58.690
And this is very much true as well given that
half the content on TikTok is just thirst

00:06:58.690 --> 00:06:59.690
traps.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:04.050
At first, countries simply tried to talk common
sense into people, but when this proved to

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:07.180
be ineffective, they started cracking down.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:11.199
Some countries decided to punish those that
were producing this content and make examples

00:07:11.199 --> 00:07:12.199
out of them.

00:07:12.199 --> 00:07:17.849
Egypt, for example, would throw five women
in prison for simply making TikTok videos.

00:07:17.849 --> 00:07:21.330
One of these women was literally arrested
for telling her followers that they could

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.910
make money by working with her.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:28.940
Fortunately, most countries didn’t go this
far, and they simply stopped at banning the

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:32.069
app like Indonesia, Bangladesh, and Pakistan.

00:07:32.069 --> 00:07:37.870
But, wait a minute, isn’t China also not
a fan of such unproductive content?

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:43.860
Well, yes, and that’s why they would crackdown
as well, but fortunately for ByteDance, they

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.450
wouldn’t go as far as banning the app.

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:50.819
Instead, they simply wanted the ByteDance
to reduce its addictiveness and spread more

00:07:50.819 --> 00:07:53.020
positive productive content.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:58.870
ByteDance would abide and this is what led
to Douyin and TikTok becoming completely different

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.150
platforms.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:05.210
While the apps’ functionality is identical,
the content is radically different.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:10.110
If you’re a kid in China, you’re daily
usage of Douyin is limited to 40 minutes,

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:14.990
and all the content that your shown will center
on science experiments and museums.

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:21.030
One social media analyst describes the difference
between Douyin and TikTok as spinach vs opium.

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:25.960
But, TikTok wasn’t just shortening attentions
and getting people arrested.

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:30.639
Given the insane popularity of the app, it
didn’t take long for bad players to start

00:08:30.639 --> 00:08:32.360
leveraging the platform.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:37.719
In late 2019 for example, the Islamic State
started using TikTok to spread their beliefs.

00:08:37.719 --> 00:08:43.070
They posted content that showed them capturing
people and even beheadings.

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:47.610
Around the same time, TikTok also became a
breeding ground for misinformation relating

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:50.660
to Covid 19 and the 2020 election.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:56.420
Things got so bad that TikTok had to go in
and delete 340,000 videos about the 2020 election

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:59.060
and 50,000 videos about Covid 19.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:04.149
2 years later, it doesn’t seem like things
have gotten much better on TikTok.

00:09:04.149 --> 00:09:09.220
NewsGuard found that as much as 20% of news
based content on TikTok contained some form

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.380
of misinformation.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:16.320
Clearly, this war against misinformation is
very much ongoing, but it didn’t take long

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:21.740
for countries to realize that all of this
unproductive content was just a singular battle,

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:22.980
a distraction.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:27.700
The real war was the cyber war against China.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:35.130
BANS PHASE 2:
The idea that TikTok collects a bunch of user

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:38.810
data is not a theory, it’s a fact.

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:43.950
It’s actually blatantly specified in their
privacy policy on their official website.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.790
Here’s some of the information that they
collect.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:53.000
IP Address, location data, keystroke patterns,
mobile carrier, and even biometric data including

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.380
faceprints and voiceprints.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:00.000
They also analyze all of the videos that are
posted on the platform to gather further information

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.190
about location and the people in the video.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:07.829
And those are just the variables that TikTok
openly admits to collecting.

00:10:07.829 --> 00:10:12.190
In the past, TikTok has gone as far as trying
to hack through Apple’s privacy policy to

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:13.450
collect more data.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:17.500
They have also successfully bypassed Google’s
security protocol.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:23.390
Fortunately, Apple and Google did catch onto
this, but that just goes to show how far TikTok

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:24.930
is willing to go.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:30.510
And the reality is that if TikTok was truly
just trying to serve the most relevant content

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:35.829
and make the most amount of money possible,
they wouldn’t go to such extents because

00:10:35.829 --> 00:10:41.200
they wouldn’t want to risk getting banned
by Apple or Google and risk long term revenue.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:45.140
But, given that they’re willing to risk
the future of the company on collecting more

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:49.019
data, their intentions become a lot more shady.

00:10:49.019 --> 00:10:52.829
And it didn’t take long for evidence to
start popping up.

00:10:52.829 --> 00:10:58.420
In August of 2022, for example, Forbes revealed
that 300 current TikTok and ByteDance employees

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.180
had previously worked for Chinese state media.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:06.139
While this is suspicious in its own right,
the story doesn’t end there.

00:11:06.139 --> 00:11:12.250
For obvious reasons, TikTok was not a fan
of Forbes exposing this information, so they

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:17.180
started spying on Forbes journalists to try
to identity their sources.

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:20.740
Ironically, Forbes would end up writing a
story about this as well.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:25.810
And craziest part is that TikTok didn’t
even try to deny the claims.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:30.779
They admitted that yes, some of their employees
had been spying on Forbes journalists.

00:11:30.779 --> 00:11:36.600
However, according to TikTok, these employees
acted on their own accord and do not represent

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.100
the company’s actions.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.990
But, you can take that for what you will.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:45.019
Also, everything that we’re covering is
simply public info.

00:11:45.019 --> 00:11:49.690
Organizations like the CIA likely have a lot
more dirt on TikTok.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:55.210
But then, why wasn’t TikTok banned 2.5 years
ago in the US along with countries like India.

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:57.810
Well, the answer is politics.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:03.980
2.5 years ago, the 2020 election was just
around the corner, and Democrats couldn’t

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:07.420
risk agreeing with Donald Trump as that could
sway swing voters.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:11.380
Also, I’m not picking on the Democratic
party specifically.

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:16.051
If Democrats were in power and they proposed
a TikTok ban, the republicans wouldn’t have

00:12:16.051 --> 00:12:18.339
risked agreeing with the Democrats either.

00:12:18.339 --> 00:12:23.170
The Republicans would’ve probably framed
a TikTok ban as some sort of attack against

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:24.550
free speech.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:29.610
And these party politics gave TikTok the perfect
oppurtunity to double down.

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:34.050
It wasn’t until after Joe Biden revoked
Trump’s TikTok ban that TikTok started collecting

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:37.260
biometric data and trying to bypass Apple’s
security.

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:43.720
So, it looks like there’s no one to blame
for TikTok’s power other than our own government.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:50.889
AN INEVITABLE BAN:
At this point, the evidence against TikTok

00:12:50.889 --> 00:12:55.070
is becoming irrefutable and the midterm elections
are over.

00:12:55.070 --> 00:13:00.339
So, it looks like both sides of Congress are
finally starting to take action and do what

00:13:00.339 --> 00:13:02.260
they deem is appropriate.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.529
This appears to include banning TikTok altogether.

00:13:05.529 --> 00:13:09.390
So far, they’ve only banned TikTok across
government organizations.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:15.420
But, it’s only been one month since that
starting addressing this threat, so its more

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:19.700
than likely that more bans and restrictions
are around the corner.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:24.140
And while you can argue all you want that
ByteDance isn’t doing anything that American

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:29.130
companies already weren’t doing, the reality
is that the US would rather have American

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:31.910
companies have this data than Chinese companies.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:37.490
So, if you’re an avid TikTok user, you might
wanna get used to Instagram Reels and YouTube

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:43.020
Shorts because the era of TikTok may soon
be coming to an end.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.010
Would you support a TikTok ban?

